laurel 2900: console head buffer, live log from byte 0, persistent boot log (port of negroni 0367).

- The first 1 MiB of console text of every boot is kept in a head buffer that is never overwritten;
  sweet_log_copy serves bytes the 4 MiB ring lost from it (a marker line covers a gap).
- Live log (raw frames and ue0): starts at byte 0 once a frame from 192.168.7.1 came (before that the
  host has no address and the datagrams were lost: the early kernel lines were missing); a failed
  sock_send keeps its bytes; "log" resends everything from byte 0. In a panic the 10 s fallback stays.
- Boot log: negroni 0367 slot area (8 slots x (header + 4 MiB ring), superblock "NEGRBLOG") at userdata
  block N-28673, the same layout, so op10tool bootlog reads it unchanged. Self-check: the HFS+ volume
  must end below the area; then a write gate opens for the area only (no ufsrw=1 needed). Header: boot
  counter, state (running/panic/halt/restart), SpringBoard mark, kernel UUID/version, boot-args, PM6125
  PON reasons of this power-on (why the boot before ended). Panic: polled write before the USB panic
  hold. Halt/restart and the USB reset/poweroff commands write the end state.
- USB commands "bootlog" and "bootlog read A C" (NBLD datagrams), /dev/laurelbootlog (root, 0400).
- Line: LAUREL BOOTLOG: on: area at partition block ... | LAUREL BOOTLOG: off: <reason>; kill switch
  laurelbootlog=0. The topaz single area (SWEETLOG, ufsrw=1) is written only when the boot log is off.

